ines‘‚¤textÙNMy covenant will I not break, nor alter the thing that is gone out of my lips.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@Once have I sworn by my holiness that I will not lie unto David.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book§chapterY«first_verse$ªlast_verse%¦verses’„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤text¿His seed shall endure for ever,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And his throne as the sun before me.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-It shall be established for ever as the moon,¦layout ‚¤textÙ+And as a faithful witness in heaven. Selah.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse%…¤book§chapterY«first_verse&ªlast_verse-¦verses˜„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ$But thou hast cast off and abhorred,¦layout ‚¤textÙ)Thou hast been wroth with thine anointed.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ0Thou hast made void the covenant of thy servant:¦layout ‚¤textÙ9Thou hast profaned his crown by casting it to the ground.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%Thou hast broken down all his hedges;¦layout ‚¤textÙ+Thou hast brought his strong holds to ruin.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#All that pass by the way spoil him:¦layout ‚¤textÙ#He is a reproach to his neighbours.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ3Thou hast set up the right hand of his adversaries;¦layout ‚¤textÙ*Thou hast made all his enemies to rejoice.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,Thou hast also turned the edge of his sword,¦layout ‚¤textÙ-And hast not made him to stand in the battle.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"Thou hast made his glory to cease,¦layout ‚¤textÙ'And cast his throne down to the ground.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ*The days of his youth hast thou shortened:¦layout ‚¤textÙ(Thou hast covered him with shame. Selah.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse-…¤book§chapte